  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 4901.02 Scope",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 4901.02 Scope.\n\n(a) These rules shall establish a voluntary certification program for certifying the following:\n\n(1) Individuals engaged in the installation of heating equipment systems or domestic water heating systems or appliances using heating oil; and\n\n(2) Individuals engaged in the servicing and repair of heating equipment or domestic water heating systems or appliances using heating oil.\n\n(b) No person shall hold him or herself as a certified oil heating technician unless the certification was obtained pursuant to these rules.\n\n(c) No person less than 18 years of age shall be issued a certificate pursuant to these rules.\n\n(d) Any person certified as an oil heating technician pursuant to these rules shall be deemed to be a qualified individual as defined in NFPA 31, Standard for the Installation of Oil Burning Equipment, as adopted in the State Fire Code, Saf-C 6000.\n\nSource. #8650, eff 6-2-06; ss by #9766-A, eff 8-3-10",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c4900.html"
